WEBVTT

00:00:00.476 --> 00:00:02.705
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> <b>How to make London more friendly</b>

00:00:22.757 --> 00:00:29.107
London is the least friendly city in the UK, or that’s what a recent survey says.

00:00:30.351 --> 00:00:34.372
I’ve lived in London all my life, and I love my city,

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:40.891
but it’s true that in a big city people aren’t always as friendly as they could be.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.855
So what can we do to get a better reputation?

00:00:45.913 --> 00:00:47.698
Here are my six tips.

00:00:48.886 --> 00:00:52.368
The first tip is for commuters on the London Underground,

00:00:52.855 --> 00:00:56.349
and it is: be understanding of other people.

00:00:57.252 --> 00:01:00.918
Not everybody uses the Tube every day to go to work,

00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:03.599
so not everybody knows the rules,

00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:11.174
for example, on an escalator, stand on the right, but walk up or down on the left.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:15.202
Some people are on the Tube because they’re tourists

00:01:15.266 --> 00:01:17.218
who want to go to Buckingham Palace.

00:01:17.821 --> 00:01:23.026
So be understanding! Don’t make a face at them – smile!

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:30.796
My second tip is for local people like me, or anybody who knows London well.

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:36.022
If a tourist asks you for directions, be patient.

00:01:36.604 --> 00:01:41.195
You’re very lucky that they are making an effort to speak to you in English.

00:01:42.062 --> 00:01:46.131
We British mostly can’t speak any other language than our own.

00:01:46.825 --> 00:01:51.198
When we’re abroad we expect other people to understand us,

00:01:51.499 --> 00:01:54.242
and most of the time, they’ll give it a try.

00:01:55.068 --> 00:01:59.735
So when they ask you for help, be patient and help them.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:03.238
Repeat the directions if necessary.

00:02:03.858 --> 00:02:07.026
Maybe even try to learn another language!

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.160
My third tip is for car drivers.

00:02:11.752 --> 00:02:13.360
Try to relax.

00:02:13.975 --> 00:02:16.441
Yes, you are stuck in a traffic jam.

00:02:16.935 --> 00:02:18.475
We know it’s frustrating.

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:21.515
But honking your horn doesn’t help anyone.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.416
It just makes people feel worse.

00:02:25.046 --> 00:02:28.588
Relax, maybe even listen to a podcast!

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:33.086
Tip number four is for London cyclists.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.238
Please stop riding on the pavement.

00:02:36.741 --> 00:02:41.344
Also, stop doing all the other things you do which annoy people,

00:02:41.542 --> 00:02:44.128
like not stopping at red traffic lights.

00:02:44.588 --> 00:02:48.573
Yes, we know you’re saving the planet, and that’s lovely.

00:02:49.007 --> 00:02:51.373
But you still need to obey the rules.

00:02:52.045 --> 00:02:55.409
Oh, and this goes for e-scooters, too!

00:02:56.836 --> 00:03:03.044
Tip number five is for residents, that’s all the people who actually live in London.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.636
Talk to your neighbours!

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:10.491
We Londoners are famous for not getting to know the people who live near us.

00:03:10.978 --> 00:03:15.824
But many of us started chatting to strangers during the COVID-19 pandemic,

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.331
and even got to know our neighbours for the first time.

00:03:20.136 --> 00:03:23.532
It’s one of the things that helped everyone to feel better,

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.172
so don’t forget about it now!

00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:30.333
My final tip is for tourists.

00:03:31.078 --> 00:03:33.101
We’re very happy to have you,

00:03:33.593 --> 00:03:37.162
but please think about the people who live and work here.

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:39.855
Help to make their lives easier.

00:03:40.418 --> 00:03:43.902
Don’t walk in busy streets with enormous suitcases

00:03:44.084 --> 00:03:47.633
or take selfies at the entrance of busy railway stations

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.448
just when commuters are trying to catch their train.

00:03:51.046 --> 00:03:54.359
Don’t walk in big groups along crowded pavements.

00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:58.111
You’ll soon see that local people will be more friendly!